post_install() {
  cat <<'TEXT'
Ghost runtime is installed without the Ghost HUD. Enable the daemon in the
current graphical session with:

  systemctl --user enable --now ghostd.service
  ghost status

The runtime keeps the CLI, authenticated API, desktop helper, and the relay
that the Ghost browser extension pairs with. The extension itself is a
separate install: https://github.com/ferdousbhai/ghost-chromium-extension
(pairing: `ghost browser allow <code>`). An app can supply its own UI.
See /usr/share/doc/ghost/ARCH.md for UI installation and removal.

Ghost homes, credentials, and state belong to you; package removal preserves them.
TEXT
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'TEXT'
Ghost runtime was upgraded. Restart it in the graphical user's session:

  systemctl --user reenable --now ghostd.service

Ghost homes, credentials, and state were preserved.
TEXT
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'TEXT'
Before removing the runtime, stop it from the graphical user's session:

  systemctl --user disable --now ghostd.service

Removal preserves ghost homes, credentials, and state.
TEXT
}
